warning[P2G3001]: the type of `$row` could not be inferred, so it stays a
    dynamic `perlval.Value`
  --> logwatch.pl:61:9
   |
61 |         $row = $parsed ? $parsed->{fields} : $raw;
   |         ^^^^
   |
   = converted: the variable and everything it flows into carry `perlval.Value`;
                the conflicting uses are in the report
   = cost: every use goes through run-time dispatch, so the compiler cannot
           check it and a wrong use is a panic
   = try: give the variable one consistent type, or annotate the sub's
          parameters, and convert again
   = learn: static-types-and-zero-values
            (perl2go explain static-types-and-zero-values)
   = learn: type-assertions-and-switches
            (perl2go explain type-assertions-and-switches)
